s": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadAudio"}, "order": 4}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#008181", "widgets_values": ["H3 MOTION CONTEXT - QUICK START\n\nThis workflow chains clips so motion AND audio continue across joins.\n\nFIRST CLIP OF A CHAIN (nothing to continue from yet):\n- Leave the H3 Motion Context group enabled\n- Load, Save, and Chain must stay in that group or the buttons do nothing\n- Load 0 / Save 1, then Run/Re-roll or Chain from there\n- Run/Re-roll queues this slot (use it instead of ComfyUI's Run). Approve advances and runs the next clip.\n\nEVERY CLIP AFTER THAT:\n- Approve on H3 Motion Context Chain, or set Load = previous, Save = now\n  (making clip 2 from clip 1: Load = 1, Save = 2)\n- Do not use queue run-on-change to bump the indices.\n\nThe saved latent carries BOTH picture and sound, so you do not need to\nload the previous clip's video from disk. Wire nothing into\ncontext_frames.\n\nDON'T LIKE THE RESULT? Click Run/Re-roll. Change nothing else.\nThe retry reloads the previous clip and overwrites its own reject.\n\nWhen you LIKE it: click Approve. That advances Load/Save and queues the\nnext clip once. Chain is Approve on a loop. At 0/1 with no clip 1 it generates\nclip 1 first; otherwise it advances then keeps going. segments is\nhow many clips that loop runs (0 = until Stop). Reset sets Load 0 /\nSave 1. Clear latents deletes numbered slots only.\n\nSETTINGS THAT WORK (tested):\ncontext_length \"22\", audio_context_length 24.\n24 frames is exactly one second of sound, and any\nmultiple of 3 lands exactly on the audio grid.\nThose are the only two settings on the node. Everything else that used\nto be exposed had one right answer and is now fixed in code.\n\nConcatenate the trimmed clips with a plain butt join - no crossfade\nneeded. Latents save to output/h3_context/\n(clip_00001.safetensors = clip 1).\n\nDark Blue Headers: H3 Motion Context nodes\nGreen Headers: nodes that need a number changed between clips\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Video context length is a dropdown: 5, 22, 39 or 56 frames. Those are\n  the only lengths the model's video latent can represent exactly.\n  Start at 22.\n- Audio context length is any number of frames up to the full clip.\n  Capture only as much as you need to carry the sound forward.\n- The pinned frames come back at the START of the new clip and the Trim\n  node removes them, so a chained clip is 22 frames (0.92s) shorter than\n  it was generated. Any timing you write into the prompt lands against\n  the longer version, so a beat written for 4.0s arrives at 3.08s in the\n  file.\n- Turn Spectrum off. Turbo LoRAs also cost you audio quality. If a chain\n  sounds duller or closer than you expected, try those before blaming\n  the chaining.\n\nIf you have rgthree installed, the Fast Group Bypasser node makes the\nmute/unmute step one click."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [510, 860], "pos": [-3440, 5540], "id": 181, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 5}, {"outputs": [{"name": "width", "links": [378], "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "width"}, {"name": "height", "links": [379], "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "height"}], "color": "#346434", "widgets_values": ["9:16 (Portrait Widescreen)", 0.4, 32], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "preview", "label": "preview", "type": "RESOLUTION_PREVIEW", "localized_name": "preview"}, {"widget": {"name": "aspect_ratio"}, "name": "aspect_ratio", "label": "aspect_ratio", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "aspect_ratio"}, {"widget": {"name": "megapixels"}, "name": "megapixels", "label": "megapixels", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "megapixels"}, {"widget": {"name": "multiple"}, "name": "multiple", "label": "multiple", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "multiple"}], "flags": {}, "type": "ResolutionSelector", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [32