et": {"name": "denoise"}, "name": "denoise", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "降噪"}], "flags": {}, "type": "BasicScheduler", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [260, 110], "pos": [-2055.451904296875, 3483.92724609375], "id": 280, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.28.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "BasicScheduler"}, "order": 26}, {"outputs": [{"name": "VIDEO", "links": [514], "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "视频"}], "color": "#006691", "widgets_values": ["LTX23Oasis_00096_.mp4", "image", "0", "image"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "file"}, "name": "file", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "文件"}, {"widget": {"name": "keep_audio"}, "name": "keep_audio", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "keep_audio"}, {"widget": {"name": "trim_time"}, "name": "trim_time", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "trim_time"}, {"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "type": "IMAGEUPLOAD", "localized_name": "选择要上传的文件"}], "flags": {}, "type": "LoadVideo", "mode": 4, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [410, 370], "pos": [-3315.879150390625, 4687.31982421875], "id": 252, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadVideo"}, "order": 11}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#008181", "widgets_values": ["H3 MOTION CONTEXT + REFERENCE MODE - QUICK START\n\nSame chaining as the T2V setup, with reference images, video or audio\nsteering the look. Your references are kept and the continuation audio\nis added alongside them. Nothing to configure for that.\n\nNeeds H3 Motion Context from August 2026 or later. Older versions\nrefused to run reference mode and chaining together.\n\nWIRING:\nMiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo -> H3 Motion Context -> guider / sampler\nReferences go on the reference node as usual. Motion Context sits after\nit and leaves them alone.\n\nFIRST CLIP OF A CHAIN:\n- Leave the H3 Motion Context group enabled\n- Load, Save, and Chain must stay in that group or the buttons do nothing\n- Load 0 / Save 1, then Run/Re-roll or Chain from there\n\nEVERY CLIP AFTER THAT:\n- Approve, or set Load = previous and Save = now\n- Keep the same references wired as the previous clip\n\nRetry and index handling are identical to the T2V note above:\nRun/Re-roll repeats a slot; Approve walks forward; Chain is Approve on a loop.\nReset sets Load 0 / Save 1. Clear latents deletes numbered slots.\nsegments is how many clips Chain runs (0 = until Stop).\n\nSETTINGS THAT WORK (tested):\ncontext_length \"22\", audio_context_length 24.\n24 frames is exactly one second of sound, and any\nmultiple of 3 lands exactly on the audio grid.\n\nPROMPTING IS THE HARD PART HERE. Read this bit.\n\nThe pinned frames are not a suggestion. They are re-injected at every\nsampling step and the model cannot render anything else in that span.\nSo if the prompt for clip 2 opens describing something different from\nhow clip 1 ended, the model does not choose between them - it renders\nBOTH. Clip 1 ends on a close-up of one character, clip 2 opens asking\nfor a two-shot of two others, and you get three people in the frame.\n\nThe fix: open every prompt by describing how the PREVIOUS clip ended.\nSame person, same clothes, same framing, same action. Let that run for\na beat past the join, then change to whatever you actually want. The\npinned frames get a stretch of timeline that agrees with them, and the\nchange happens where nothing is pinned.\n\nGive the hold something to do - a breath, a weight shift, an eyeline\nchange. A held framing with nothing happening in it renders as a frozen\nframe and looks like the video stalled.\n\nAt 22 frames of context the pin is 0.92s, and you want a beat past that,\nso plan on the change landing around 1.5 to 2 seconds in. On a 5 second\nclip that is most of the first half. Longer clips are easier than a\nshorter hold.\n\nREFERENCES HAVE NO TIMING. Every reference conditions the whole clip.\nThere is no way to say \"this one applies from two seconds in.\" If the\noutfit, location or character changes partway through, the shot\nstructure and the description have to carry that on their own.\n\nDark Blue Headers: H3 Motion Context nodes\nGreen Headers: nodes that need a user input between clips"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [510, 940], "pos": [-4240, 4201.51611328125], "id": 246, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 12}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"name": "images", "links": [444], "label": "images", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"name": "audio", "links": [445], "label": "audio", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "音频"}, {"name": "fps", "label": "fps", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "帧率"}, {"name": "bit_depth", "label": "bit_depth", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "bit_depth"}, {"name": "color_space", "label": "color_space", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "color_space"}], "size": [200, 110], "pos": [-2800, 4660], "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "video", "link": 514, "label": "video", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "视频"}], "flags": {"collapsed": false}, "id": 242, "type": "GetVideoComponents", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "GetVideoComponents"}, "order": 21}, {"outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [512], "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"name": "MASK", "label": "遮罩", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "遮罩"}], "color": "#006691", "widgets_values": ["pasted/802124e30e04c984fed60efeeb8e3a041bf5269b7af61ef11d5f7f4eae53d198.png", "image"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "image"}, "name": "image", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "type": "IMAGEUPLOAD", "localized_name": "选择文件上传"}], "flags": {}, "type": "LoadImage", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [300, 410], "pos": [-2900, 5070], "id": 250, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "order": 13}, {"outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [513], "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"name": "MASK", "label": "遮罩", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "遮罩"}], "color": "#006691", "widgets_values": ["pasted/d624fb9a40312862618a94aa36ef50c93edd271d37736463740e6a7042792830.png", "image"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "image"}, "name": "image", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "type": "IMAGEUPLOAD", "localized_name": "选择文件上传"}], "flags": {}, "type": "LoadImage", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [300, 410], "pos": [-2580, 5070], "id": 251, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.30.2", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "order": 14}, {"outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [382], "label": "字符串", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "字符串"}], "color": "#346434", "widgets_values": ["subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the freckled red-haired boy superhero from <Picture 1>, with a black eye mask, a black suit with a large white chest star, red boots and a flowing red cape. Preserve his identity and costume.\n<Subject 2> is the colossal black armored mech-kaiju from <Picture 2>, with red glowing eyes, a bright red chest core, jagged mechanical jaws and thin blue lightning above its head. Preserve its silhouette and armor.\n<Subject 3> is the wet rooftop and dark blue-black night city from <Picture 1>, with red window reflections and heavy comic ink shading.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A continuous comic-book camera move across <Subject 3>, showing <Subject 1> and revealing <Subject 2> beyond the skyline. Bold ink outlines, red accents and blue-black shadows.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in\n[Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep the boy's face, mask, suit, star emblem and red cape from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep the mech's red core, black armored body and blue lightning from <Picture 2>.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - reuse the wet roof, city, reflected red light and comic ink style from <Picture 1>.\n\ndetailed_description:\nBold comic-book ink illustration in motion, with sharp heavy black linework, red and blue-black colors, wet rooftop reflections and stable nighttime lighting.\n[Shot 1] A single unbroken shot. Begin high above <Subject 1>, who stands firmly on the rooftop with his hands on his hips and his face looking up toward the lens. His red hair, freckles, black mask and white chest star are clearly readable. His cape billows continuously to screen right in the wind, its hem making slow rolling folds. The camera slowly descends and smoothly starts a clockwise orbit around the boy, maintaining the same speed throughout the shot. The rooftop parapet and red-lit buildings glide sideways with coherent parallax. <Subject 2> stands beyond the distant skyline in the right background, initially partly hidden behind buildings, with a steady red chest glow and fine blue electric arcs. During the middle of the shot, <Subject 1> (S1) smiles confidently and says with a bright youthful male voice, <d>[English] Get ready to meet your maker!</d>. His lips match the complete line. White jagged comic letters with black outlines and small red shadows appear above his shoulder in sync: \"GET READY TO\", then \"MEET\", then \"YOUR\", then \"MAKER\". The words dissipate before the end of the shot. After finishing the line he closes his mouth and gradually turns his gaze toward the distant mech. Continue the descending clockwise camera orbit and the cape's existing wind motion through the final frame. The mech's chest brightens slightly and a low mechanical rumble gradually rises. Keep the boy on the roof, stable scale and proportions, and carry the same motion into the end of this continuous shot.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous rooftop wind, soft cape flapping, distant city ambience and the rising low mechanical rumble from the distant mech. The boy's voice is clear and close while the wind and city remain underneath it.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA continuous sparse cinematic electronic pulse at a steady 96 BPM, low bass and soft percussion, building slowly without a musical ending or fade at the end of the shot.\n\n---\n\n[Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep the boy's face, mask, suit, star emblem and red cape from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - keep the mech's red core, black armored body and blue lightning from <Picture 2>.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - reuse the wet roof, city, reflected red light and comic ink style from <Picture 1>.\n\ndetailed_description:\nBold comic-book ink illustration in motion, with the same heavy black linework, red and blue-black palette, wet rooftop reflections and nighttime lighting.\n[Shot 1] Continue the ongoing shot from the supplied opening motion context. The opening context already shows <Subject 1> on the rooftop, his mouth closed after his finished line, looking toward <Subject 2>, with his cape blowing to screen right. Maintain the exact continuing pose, camera direction, scale, lighting and cape movement from this opening context. Continue the camera's existing slow clockwise orbit and downward drift at the same speed, without restarting the motion. Let the rooftop parapet and red-lit buildings continue their coherent sideways parallax. The boy remains in the foreground and gradually moves toward the left third as the camera's continuous orbit reveals more of <Subject 2> beyond the skyline on the right. The boy steadily turns his head a little farther toward the mech, his feet stay planted and his hands remain on his hips. His red cape continues its existing flutter rather than settling or restarting. The colossal black mech slowly lifts its head and leans slightly forward above the buildings, its red eyes and chest core steadily intensifying and blue lightning crackling along its head. Its mechanical jaws open gradually and <Subject 2> (S2) produces a deep resonant nonverbal roar, rising naturally out of the rumble already heard in the opening context. Keep the boy visible on the rooftop, the mech in the same background location and the city geometry coherent. The view remains one unbroken camera move. Continue the wind and low electronic pulse through the roar and sustain the scene's motion to the end. The boy remains silent throughout this continuation; his earlier line and comic letters have already finished.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nCarry the ongoing rooftop wind, cape flapping and distant city ambience through the opening context into the new action. Continue the existing low mech rumble smoothly, building it into a deep mechanical roar with a light crackle of blue electricity. Preserve the ambient noise level across the context boundary.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nContinue the same sparse cinematic electronic pulse at a steady 96 BPM, retaining the existing bass texture and beat phase from the opening audio context, under the wind and mechanical roar."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "文本"}], "flags": {}, "type": "Text Multiline", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)", "size": [620, 370], "pos": [-2502.777099609375, 4618.509765625], "id": 220, "properties": {"cnr_id": "was-ns", "ver": "3.0.1", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Text Multiline"}, "order": 15}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "positive", "links": [425], "label": "positive", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "positive"}, {"name": "LATENT", "links": [427, 599], "label": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "Latent"}], "size": [320, 430], "pos": [-1820.89306640625, 4237.63720703125], "widgets_values": ["", 1344, 768, 124, "match"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 594, "lab